# Project Rules

- Use React + Vite + TypeScript for all UI work.
- Follow the existing app structure and keep components in the current folders.
- Prefer reusable components and keep logic clean and readable.
- Use Tailwind utility classes for styling whenever possible.
- Keep imports organized and avoid unused variables.
- Use double quotes for strings when needed, and avoid broken JSX or unclosed tags.
- Preserve the current design system: dark navy and green accent palette, clean modern medical branding.
- Keep code simple, production-ready, and consistent with the existing app patterns.
- Do not add unnecessary dependencies or large refactors without reason.
- Prefer functional React components and hooks, using default exports for components.
- When editing pages or shared components, maintain the existing layout, spacing, and visual style.
- Ensure accessibility: valid button labels, semantic structure, and clear interactive states.
- For API work, keep calls centralized in the existing API layer and handle loading/error states cleanly.
- Before finalizing code, check for TypeScript or JSX errors and fix them.
